load @term/seed/theory/category
  find category

# A morphism: an arrow of a category, a structure-preserving map from one object to another, the second primitive of
# category theory after the object. Morphisms compose associatively and each object has an identity morphism. What an
# object is is determined entirely by its morphisms. The form carries the category the morphism lives in.
form morphism
  link category, like category
